Looking at the failure case peer-b26, I need to trace the state transitions:

- peer-b24: startBtn=TRUE, pv=100 → phase=1 (new start)
- peer-b25: startBtn=TRUE (held), pv=100 → phase=2 (pv reached setpoint)
- peer-b26: startBtn=FALSE, pv=20, prev phase=2, elapsed=1

The observed phase=1 but should be phase=2. The issue is my code allows reverting from phase=2 back to phase=1 when pv < setpoint. PUB008 says "保温阶段始终维持到超时、中止或新启动" — holding phase persists until timeout/abort/new start, regardless of pv.

```json
{"edits":[{"old":"    ELSIF (tmp_prevPhase = 1) OR (tmp_prevPhase = 2) THEN
    // PUB009: running phase → increment elapsed, then evaluate timeout/transition
    elapsed := elapsed + 1;
    IF elapsed >= maxDuration THEN
        // PUB010: timeout reached → complete; pv check skipped
        timeout := TRUE;
        phase   := 3;
    ELSIF pv >= setpoint THEN
        phase := 2;
    ELSE
        phase := 1;
    END_IF;", "new":"    ELSIF (tmp_prevPhase = 1) OR (tmp_prevPhase = 2) THEN
    // PUB009: running phase → increment elapsed, then evaluate timeout/transition
    elapsed := elapsed + 1;
    IF elapsed >= maxDuration THEN
        // PUB010: timeout reached → complete; pv check skipped
        timeout := TRUE;
        phase   := 3;
    ELSIF tmp_prevPhase = 1 THEN
        // phase 1 → 2 on setpoint reached; otherwise stay in 1
        IF pv >= setpoint THEN
            phase := 2;
        ELSE
            phase := 1;
        END_IF;
    ELSE
        // PUB008: phase 2 (holding) persists until timeout/abort/new start
        phase := 2;
    END_IF;"}]}
```
